Notebook[{
Cell["Why Boson Sampling Is Hard", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
Two-photon interference, normalized permanent amplitudes, classical \
computation, and the assumptions behind sampling hardness: a \
computation-first narrative with the Wolfram Language and QuantumFramework\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: Oct 22, 2026)", "Author",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research Inc, USA", "Affiliation",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Modes, Occupation Lists, and Assumptions", "Section",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["occupation list",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " records the photon count in each of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " modes, with one entry per mode. Here, each input or output mode \
corresponds to a port of the optical network. An ",
 StyleBox["input occupation list",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " specifies how many photons enter each input port; an ",
 StyleBox["output occupation list",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " specifies how many photons are detected at each output port. The \
occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " labels the Fock state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
We will follow two photons through a beam splitter, derive the normalized \
permanent amplitude, compare ways of computing it, and examine what this says \
about classical sampling. Computing one amplitude, collecting every \
probability, and drawing one sample are different tasks; keeping them \
separate is essential to the hardness argument.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["\<\
The examples assume a passive lossless network and number-resolving \
detectors. The photons may enter different ports, but their internal wave \
packets must match in arrival time, spectrum, polarization, and unresolved \
spatial structure to interfere fully. Partial distinguishability reduces that \
interference. Loss changes the detected photon-number sectors, while \
threshold detectors merge different occupation lists into the same click \
pattern; neither alone makes the photons distinguishable.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell["\<\
Load QuantumFramework and its second-quantization tools, then evaluate the \
cells in order:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Two-Photon Interference at a Beam Splitter", "Section",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the smallest interesting case: two identical photons, one into \
each port of a single balanced beam splitter. A balanced beam splitter sends \
each incoming photon out either side with equal probability, so a classical \
intuition says the two photons land on the same side half the time and on \
opposite sides half the time. The quantum answer is stranger: the two photons \
never come out on opposite sides. They always leave together. In other words, \
the output occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ", one photon in each output mode, has probability zero. This is the \
Hong-Ou-Mandel effect, and it is the whole subject in miniature."
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build a two-mode interferometer that is a single balanced beam splitter \
(the angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " makes the reflection and transmission amplitudes equal in size):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qbs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["Draw it, so we can see the one element the photons meet:", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qbs", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything a passive network of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " modes does to a single photon is held in one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ", its transfer matrix: the entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " is the amplitude for a photon entering port ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " to leave port ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 ". For the beam splitter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ", and we store its matrix as ",
 Cell[BoxData["Wbs"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["Read the transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Wbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"qbs", "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Wbs", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the four entries are equal in magnitude but not in sign: one \
of them carries a minus. That sign is not decoration. It is the seed of the \
interference, and we are about to watch it cancel an entire outcome.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ask ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " for the full distribution over output occupation lists when one photon \
enters each port, giving the input occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qbs", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the output occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " has probability zero, while the two bunched output occupation lists ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " split the probability between them. The photons leave together, every \
time. The next question is where that zero comes from, and the cleanest way \
to see it is to compute the same three numbers for three different kinds of \
particle and read them side by side."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["Occupation Lists and the Permanent Formula", "Subsection",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To compare the three particle types, we need the ",
 StyleBox["permanent",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of a square matrix. It is defined like the determinant, as a sum over all \
ways of pairing rows with columns, except that every term is added with a \
plus sign where the determinant alternates the signs."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell["\<\
The probability helpers below assume valid input and output occupation lists \
with the same positive total photon count.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a helper, ",
 Cell[BoxData["modeList"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ", that converts an input or output occupation list into a ",
 StyleBox["mode assignment list",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a list containing the mode label once for each photon in that mode. \
Replace each count ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " copies of the mode label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", then join the groups into one list. For example,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", "0", ",", 
   RowBox[{
   "1", "}", "\[ThickSpace]", "\[LongRightArrow]", "\[ThickSpace]", "{", "{", 
    "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
   "{", "3", "}", "}", "\[ThickSpace]", "\[LongRightArrow]", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    "{", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "}"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["\<\
The occupation list has one entry per mode; the mode assignment list has one \
entry per photon. These entries are bookkeeping for the occupied modes and do \
not make the photons distinguishable.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "modeList", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "occ_List", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Catenate", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], " ", 
      "&"}], ",", " ", "occ"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell["Name the three output occupation lists we are comparing:", "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"outs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For indistinguishable bosons, let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " be the input and output occupation lists, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", since a passive lossless network neither creates nor destroys photons. \
Define ",
 Cell[BoxData["bosonProb"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " to compute the probability of observing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " and the transfer matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "bosonProb", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bosonProb", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
      RowBox[{"w", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
     "2"}], " ", "/", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To unpack this calculation, start with the device's transfer matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ", whose entries are single-photon amplitudes. The input mode assignment \
list selects columns, and the output mode assignment list selects rows: \
repeat column ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " times and row ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " times. Call the resulting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each column of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["M", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " represents an incoming photon, and each row an outgoing detection. A \
complete connection between them uses every row and column once. Because the \
photons do not interact, its contribution is the product of the corresponding \
single-photon amplitudes. For example, one contribution is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "11"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "22"], "\[CenterEllipsis]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"n", "n"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Identical bosons require us to add these contributions with no extra \
exchange signs. Summing over all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " permutations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " of the columns gives precisely the permanent:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Per",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "1"}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell["\<\
Normalizing the input and output Fock states then gives the amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LeftArrow]", 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Per",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"],
          LimitsPositioning->False], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{
        UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"],
         LimitsPositioning->False], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "!"}]}]}]]], "."}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell["\<\
The factorials account for the normalization of states with multiple photons \
in the same mode. To obtain the probability, take the squared magnitude of \
the amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LeftArrow]", 
          StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["Per",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], 
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"],
          LimitsPositioning->False], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{
        UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"],
         LimitsPositioning->False], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "!"}]}]}]], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is what ",
 Cell[BoxData["bosonProb"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " evaluates: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "...", "]"}], "^", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " takes the squared magnitude of the permanent, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " multiplies the factorials of all input and output occupation counts."
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell["Comparing Particle Statistics", "Subsection",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For classical distinguishable particles the amplitudes never interfere. \
Each photon crosses the network on its own, leaving input mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " for output mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 ", so the probability of an output occupation list is the permanent of the \
block of entrywise squared magnitudes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubsuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 ", selected by the same repeated rows and columns, divided only by the \
output factorials:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["dist",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Per",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
        {
         StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], "2"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "!"}]]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The permanent counts each assignment of photons to output modes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " times, once for every way of matching the photons in mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 " copies of row ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 ", and the output factorials remove that overcount. There is no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", because photons that start in the same mode are still different \
particles. Define that:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "distProb", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"distProb", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ")"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For indistinguishable noninteracting fermions, odd permutations contribute \
a minus sign, giving a ",
 StyleBox["determinant",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". A valid input occupation list has only zero-or-one counts; output \
collisions have probability zero. Define the probability for such inputs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "fermionProb", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fermionProb", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
     RowBox[{"w", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
    "2"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell["\<\
Put the three particle types in one table, with one row per output occupation \
list:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Bold"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<output\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<indistinguishable bosons\>\"",
          ",", " ", "\"\<distinguishable bosons\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<indistinguishable fermions\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Through", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "bosonProb", ",", " ", "distProb", ",", " ", "fermionProb"}], 
            "}"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"Wbs", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<|\>\"", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
             RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<,\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
            " ", "\"\<\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "outs"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Spacings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distinguishable probabilities are a quarter, a half, a quarter. Bosonic \
coincidence vanishes because its two contributions are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ": positive exchange coefficients do not prevent destructive interference \
between signed optical amplitudes. Fermions instead leave one particle in \
each output mode with certainty. A bunched output repeats a matrix row, \
making its determinant zero, as required by Pauli exclusion."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell["\<\
Check the coincidence amplitude at a variable beam-splitter angle:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "theta", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"splitter", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
          RowBox[{"theta", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"splitter", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "theta"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{"theta", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " this amplitude is one, restoring the input; at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " it vanishes. We can now derive the amplitude for an arbitrary passive \
network."
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell["Many-Photon Amplitudes as Normalized Permanents", "Section",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same amplitude formula follows directly from how a passive network acts \
on the creation operators. Each network sends the operator that creates a \
photon in input port ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " to a superposition over the outputs,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[ThickSpace]", "\[Function]", 
    "\[ThickSpace]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Replace the commuting creation operators by variables ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ". The transformed input is encoded by"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " collects all contributions to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 ". Restoring Fock-state normalization gives"
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LeftArrow]", 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
    SqrtBox[
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"],
         LimitsPositioning->False], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "!"}], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"],
         LimitsPositioning->False], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "!"}]]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Per",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "!"}], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["\<\
Thus coefficient extraction and the permanent formula compute the same \
complex amplitude.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To watch this on a network with no special structure, draw one at random. A \
random unitary is the natural \"generic\" network, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Random\>\"", "[", "m", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 " builds an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 "-mode one and factors it into beam splitters and phase shifters."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell["\<\
Build a random five-mode interferometer with a fixed seed, so the run is \
reproducible:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2026", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Random\>\"", "[", "5", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell["Draw the mesh the photons will cross:", "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qi", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell["Read its transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"W", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"qi", "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"W", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now use input occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ", with one photon entering each of ports 1, 2, and 3, and ask for the \
amplitude of output occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ", with one photon leaving each of ports 1, 3, and 4. The corresponding mode \
assignment lists select columns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "2", ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " and rows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"4", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ". Both occupation lists are collision-free: every count is zero or one. All \
factorials in the normalization are therefore one, so the amplitude is the \
permanent of this selected ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute that amplitude directly from ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qi", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}],
     " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell["\<\
Confirm it equals the permanent of the matrix selected by the same input and \
output occupation lists:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"in", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"out", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"qi", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"in", " ", "->", " ", "out"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
     RowBox[{"W", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "out", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "\n",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For this collision-free example, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Amplitude\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " uses the direct permanent route, so this checks selection rather than \
independently verifying the formula."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now put two photons in port 1 and one in port 3: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", "{", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 ". Choose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", "{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ". The selected columns are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " and rows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "2", ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 ", so both input and output collisions enter the normalization: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"2", "!"}]}]], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell["Check the amplitude against the normalized permanent:", "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"in", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "2", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"out", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"qi", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"in", " ", "->", " ", "out"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
        RowBox[{"W", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "out", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
       "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]}], "\n", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The formula does not prescribe an algorithm. For approximate transfer \
matrices, ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 " may group repeated occupations, using only occupied rows and columns and \
choosing the orientation with fewer summands. The grouped sum has"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["min",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", "\[ThickSpace]", 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], "}"}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "terms: six in this example, versus ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", "3"], "=", "8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " for collision-free input and output. Exact transfer matrices retain the \
direct ",
 Cell[BoxData["Permanent"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " route. These are evaluations of the same quantity; ",
 Cell[BoxData["bosonProb"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " remains our simple reference."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell["Computing and Checking the Full Output Distribution", "Section",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A physical boson sampler produces output occupation lists. To inspect the \
probabilities underlying those samples, collect the whole distribution for \
input occupation list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"probs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"qi", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["Show the five most likely output occupation lists:", "Text",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TakeLargest", "[", 
  RowBox[{"probs", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is one probability for each output occupation list. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " modes there are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " such lists, counting every way to place the photons in the modes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell["Confirm the distribution has exactly that many entries:", "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", "probs", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "5", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm it is a genuine probability distribution, summing to one (",
 Cell[BoxData["Chop"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 " sets the tiny machine-precision residue to zero so the comparison tests \
the physics, not the rounding; see ",
 ButtonBox["Chop",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Chop.html"], None}],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "probs", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
   " ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For passive Fock inputs, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Probabilities\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " obtains all amplitudes by expanding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " and extracting its coefficients, then squares their magnitudes. ",
 Cell[BoxData["FrobeniusSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " only enumerates the possible output occupation lists; it does not \
calculate amplitudes. This is a different algorithm from separately \
evaluating selected permanents."
}], "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First compare the complex amplitudes, so relative-phase errors cannot \
disappear upon squaring. The call ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"qi", "[", "in", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " returns the coefficient-based amplitude association:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"in", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
      "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"amps", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"qi", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
            RowBox[{"amps", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"QuditName", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], 
           " ", "-", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
             RowBox[{"W", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/",
             "\n", "        ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", 
               RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
                RowBox[{"in", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
          "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"FrobeniusSolve", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"10", "^", 
       RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]}], "\n", " ", "]"}]}], "\n", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell["Verify the probabilities independently as well:", "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
        RowBox[{"probs", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"QuditName", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "-",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"bosonProb", "[", 
        RowBox[{"W", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
          "}"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", "\n",
     "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FrobeniusSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], 
       "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both routes agree within numerical precision. Polynomial expansion shares \
work across outputs, but it is not automatically a polynomial-time algorithm: \
a generic expansion has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 " coefficients, which can grow exponentially when the photon and mode counts \
grow together. A separate permanent evaluation for every output is one \
approach, not a requirement. What does one generic permanent cost?"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell["The Cost of One Amplitude", "Section",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How does the cost of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"qi", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"S", " ", "->", " ", "T"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " grow with photon count? Compare three input and output occupation patterns \
in random networks with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " modes: collision-free, pairs (plus one single photon when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " is odd), and all photons in one mode. For each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 ", use the same transfer matrix for all three patterns and move the occupied \
output modes to the other half of the ports."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell["\<\
Define the input occupation lists and display them for six photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"inputOccupation", ",", " ", "patterns"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"inputOccupation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "\"\<collision-free\>\""}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"inputOccupation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "\"\<pairs\>\""}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Quotient", "[", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"inputOccupation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "\"\<bunched\>\""}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "n", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"patterns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<collision-free\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<pairs\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<bunched\>\""}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"inputOccupation", "[", 
     RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "patterns"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each point measures one evaluation after ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ", using machine-precision transfer matrices. Construct the network before \
timing; for the direct reference, also prepare the selected matrix and \
normalization first. The timer returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"seconds", ",", " ", "amplitude"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " so we can check the value as well as the cost."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell["\<\
Define the timer and the two ways to evaluate one normalized amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "singleTiming", ",", " ", "transitionTiming", ",", " ", "amplitudeCost"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SetAttributes", "[", 
   RowBox[{"singleTiming", ",", " ", "HoldAll"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"singleTiming", "[", "expr_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", "expr", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transitionTiming", "[", 
    RowBox[{"q_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_", ",", " ", "\"\<QI\>\""}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"singleTiming", "[", 
    RowBox[{"q", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "->", " ", "t"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"transitionTiming", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "q_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_", ",", " ", "\"\<Permanent\>\""}], 
     "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"matrix", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"q", "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
        "   ", 
        RowBox[{"normalization", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
             RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
       "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"singleTiming", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", "matrix", "]"}], "/", "normalization"}], 
       "]"}]}], "\n", " ", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "pattern_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"method_", ":", " ", "\"\<QI\>\""}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1107", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1000", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"q", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Random\>\"", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"inputOccupation", "[", 
           RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "pattern"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "  ", 
       RowBox[{"transitionTiming", "[", 
        RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateRight", "[", 
          RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "method"}], "]"}]}], 
      "\n", " ", "]"}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell["\<\
Confirm that the QI and direct-reference amplitudes agree for all three \
six-photon patterns:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
        RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
         RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "pattern"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
        RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
         RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "pattern", ",", " ", "\"\<Permanent\>\""}], 
         "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
     RowBox[{"10", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"pattern", ",", " ", "patterns"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Time the QI amplitudes through 28 photons. This sweep can take several \
minutes; shorten ",
 Cell[BoxData["photonCounts"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 " for a quicker run:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"photonCounts", ",", " ", "qiTimings"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"photonCounts", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "2", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "10", ",", " ", "14", ",", " ", "18", ",", 
     " ", "22", ",", " ", "24", ",", " ", "26", ",", " ", "28"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qiTimings", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"pattern", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", 
            RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
             RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "pattern"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "photonCounts"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      "\n", " ", "patterns"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell["Plot the cost of one QI amplitude against photon count:", "Text",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Values", "[", "qiTimings", "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Large"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<photons n (m = 2 n modes)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<seconds per QI amplitude\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "qiTimings", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Occupation structure changes the cost of one amplitude\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The collision-free and paired patterns become costly, while QI exploits \
repeated occupations and occupied modes to keep the fully bunched case cheap. \
Here every selected entry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ",", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ", so the normalized amplitude reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubsuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ",", "1"}], 
   RowBox[{"\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 ". This structured case does not represent a generic permanent. \
Submillisecond single-call timings are noisy; focus on the large separation \
in cost."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare QI with the default built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["Permanent"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 " at 22 photons, using the same timer and reusing the QI measurements \
above:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"pattern", ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SelectFirst", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"qiTimings", "[", "pattern", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "22"}], " ", 
             "&"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"First", "[", 
          RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
           RowBox[{"22", ",", " ", "pattern", ",", " ", "\"\<Permanent\>\""}],
            "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"pattern", ",", " ", "patterns"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<occupation pattern\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QI (seconds)\>\"", 
       ",", " ", "\"\<direct Permanent (seconds)\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The collision-free QI timings track the default ",
 Cell[BoxData["Permanent"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 ", which QI calls internally for that case. The bunched comparison shows \
what exploiting occupation structure saves."
}], "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell["\<\
Using this protocol on the machine used here (Wolfram Language 15.0, macOS \
ARM), the collision-free call took about 148 seconds at 28 photons and 295 \
seconds at 29 photons. Thus 28 is a comfortable stopping point for a \
five-minute-per-call budget here, while 29 leaves little margin. Timings vary \
with hardware and kernel version.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell["Optionally time the 29-photon collision-free amplitude:", "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"First", "[", 
  RowBox[{"amplitudeCost", "[", 
   RowBox[{"29", ",", " ", "\"\<collision-free\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a general dense complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " matrix, algorithms such as Ryser's and Glynn's take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 " arithmetic operations to evaluate its permanent, while Gaussian \
elimination evaluates its determinant in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "3"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ". These timings characterize particular implementations and occupation \
patterns. Computing a general permanent exactly is #P-hard (Valiant, 1979), a \
worst-case result that permits easy structured instances."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell["From Amplitude Cost to Sampling Hardness", "Section",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell["\<\
A hard probability calculation does not by itself establish hard sampling. A \
sampler can avoid constructing the full distribution, and even a distribution \
written using permanents may admit easy samples.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Distinguishable photons supply a counterexample. Their output probabilities \
involve permanents of entrywise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 ", yet sampling needs only independent draws from its columns: draw an \
output for each incoming photon, then count the results."
}], "Text",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that each column of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 " is a genuine probability distribution over the output modes, by checking \
that every column sums to one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "W", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell["\<\
This verifies the normalized single-photon distributions used by that \
sampler, without evaluating any permanent.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The missing bridge is a complexity result. Aaronson and Arkhipov showed \
that a polynomial-time classical algorithm for exact boson sampling would \
collapse the polynomial hierarchy to its third level, contrary to a standard \
complexity assumption. Their approximate-sampling argument additionally \
assumes average-case hardness of Gaussian permanents and permanent \
anticoncentration (",
 ButtonBox["Aaronson and Arkhipov, 2010",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.3245"], None}],
 "). These assumptions rule out polynomial-time sampling; they do not prove \
that every classical algorithm takes exponential time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original approximate-hardness argument uses a dilute regime with many \
more modes than photons, connecting optical submatrices to Gaussian random \
matrices. That is not a universal restriction: later work extends hardness \
evidence to a linear number of modes, where collisions are common (",
 ButtonBox["Bouland et al., 2026",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://journals.aps.org/prx/abstract/10.1103/xc7b-sjm5"], None}],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Classical algorithms also improve on full-distribution enumeration. \
Clifford and Clifford give exact sampling in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["poly",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 " time, with further average-case improvements in denser regimes (",
 ButtonBox["Clifford and Clifford, 2020",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.04214"], None}],
 "). Algorithmic improvements and conditional hardness coexist: the former \
exploit structure or share work, while the latter concern suitable growing \
families of instances."
}], "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell["Summary and Next Questions", "Section",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell["\<\
We have connected two-photon interference to normalized permanent amplitudes, \
checked those amplitudes and probabilities against an independent coefficient \
calculation, and measured how photon count and occupation structure affect QI \
amplitude calculations. The computations explain the optical probabilities; \
the cited complexity results supply the separate, conditional argument about \
classical sampling.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell["\<\
The next questions concern partial distinguishability, loss, and detector \
resolution, each of which changes the experiment differently. Replacing \
single-photon inputs by squeezed vacuum leads to Gaussian boson sampling, \
where hafnians take the role played here by permanents.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"
]
